{"h": {"measure": "P", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 131, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual where there was none adds a strong gradient path, whereas replacing a conv on edge 3 with skip removes capacity, so the gain is larger when skip replaces none."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 already absent, deleting edge 5 leaves node 3 fed only by edge 3, which removes nodes 1 and 2 from the output and collapses accuracy."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 5 is none, edge 4 is the only route from the intermediate nodes to the output, so removing it is much more harmful."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 4 is none, node 1 reaches the output only through edge 2 (often also none), so improving edge 0 has little or no downstream effect."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Node 2 is cut off from the output when edge 5 is none, so adding a conv on edge 1 cannot help."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Edge 2 feeds node 2, which is dead when edge 5 is none, so the conv added there has no effect on the output."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling op on the final edge with a learnable 3x3 conv gives a larger gain than replacing skip or 1x1 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the input-to-output residual hurts trainability much more than removing a conv or pool on that edge."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 0 is none, node 1 carries zero features, so a skip from node 1 to the output contributes nothing."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "In pooling-dominated cells with no learnable ops, adding a 3x3 conv supplies much-needed capacity, so the gain is larger than in conv-rich cells."}], "tok": 30497, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "a